---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "VolEq Android privacy policy | Patrik Dóczy";
const description =
  "Privacy information for VolEq - Realtime Volume Balancer and VolEq - Premium on Android: local audio effects, saved settings, and advertising in the free edition.";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} pathname="/privacy/voleq-android/">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/privacy/"
          >Privacy</a
        ><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page"
          >VolEq Android</span
        >
      </nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">Android app privacy policy</p>
      <h1>VolEq Android privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Audio processing stays on your device. The free edition uses optional
        rewarded advertising; Premium contains no advertising software.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 9 September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell content-grid">
      <aside>
        <p class="eyebrow">VolEq for Android</p>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:doczy.patrik410@gmail.com"
            >Privacy and support contact</a
          >
        </p>
        <p><a href="/privacy/voleq/">VolEq for macOS privacy policy</a></p>
        <p><a href="/privacy/">Website privacy</a></p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <div class="note">
          <p>
            This policy covers <strong>VolEq - Realtime Volume Balancer</strong> (<code
              >com.veryclevernamecompany.voleq</code
            >) and <strong>VolEq - Premium</strong> (<code
              >com.veryclevernamecompany.voleq.paid</code
            >) on Android. It covers the updated 1.7 release. The separate macOS
            application has its own policy.
          </p>
        </div>
        <h2>Developer and contact</h2>
        <p>
          Patrik Dóczy develops VolEq and is responsible for its data handling.
          Send privacy questions or requests to <a
            href="mailto:doczy.patrik410@gmail.com">doczy.patrik410@gmail.com</a
          >.
        </p>
        <h2>Audio processing and permissions</h2>
        <p>
          VolEq uses Android audio effects to balance playback volume on your
          device. It does not record, store, upload, or analyse audio on a
          server, and it does not request microphone access. Calibration plays
          bundled audio samples locally.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you start balancing, a foreground service keeps processing active
          and provides notification controls until you stop it or free-edition
          access expires. Notification permission lets Android show these
          controls. Optional display-over-other-apps permission enables the
          floating controls. You can revoke these permissions in Android
          settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          In restricted mode, VolEq receives audio-session identifiers and the
          package names supplied by compatible audio players so that it can
          attach effects to their playback. This information stays in memory
          while the service is running; VolEq does not upload it or build an
          inventory of installed apps.
        </p>
        <h2>Settings stored on your device</h2>
        <p>
          VolEq saves presets, calibration and audio-mode settings,
          floating-control position, free-edition access expiry, and local usage
          counters for review prompts and earned rewards. The app has no user
          accounts, developer-operated server, or separate analytics or
          automatic crash-reporting service.
        </p>
        <p>
          These local settings remain until you clear the app's storage or
          uninstall it. Android may include app settings in your device backup
          and restore them, depending on your system and account settings. Your
          backup provider controls that processing; Patrik does not receive the
          backup.
        </p>
        <h2>Advertising in the free edition</h2>
        <p>
          The free edition uses Google AdMob. Choosing to watch a rewarded
          advertisement can add 24 hours of balancing access after Google
          reports that the reward was earned. Ads may be prepared in advance
          after the applicable privacy checks, but full-screen ads are shown
          only when you request one.
        </p>
        <p>
          VolEq requests nonpersonalised ads and disables Google's publisher
          first-party identifier for ad personalisation. Google's advertising
          software still collects and shares network information (including IP
          address and approximate location derived from it), app/ad
          interactions, performance diagnostics, and available device or account
          identifiers for ad delivery, measurement, and fraud prevention. The
          Android advertising ID and other identifiers depend on your device
          settings and privacy choices. Advertising traffic is encrypted in
          transit.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google's User Messaging Platform obtains and manages applicable
          privacy choices. Where required, you are shown a consent form before
          an ad request. You can revisit available choices using <strong
            >Advertising privacy options</strong
          > in VolEq's information panel. Declining personalisation does not prevent
          you from using time already available. Ad availability can vary with your
          privacy choices and Google's service.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also reset or delete your advertising ID in Android settings.
          See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google's privacy policy</a
          > and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            >Google's information about partner apps</a
          > for its processing, retention, and controls. Google and its service providers
          may process data outside your country under their applicable safeguards.
        </p>
        <h2>Premium and Google Play</h2>
        <p>
          VolEq - Premium is a separate paid application with no AdMob or
          advertising-consent SDK. It does not request advertisements or impose
          the free edition's time allowance. Google Play processes the app
          purchase and associated account and payment information under its own
          privacy policy. Patrik does not receive your payment-card details. An
          optional Google Play review prompt is handled by Google Play.
        </p>
        <h2>Optional support reports and external links</h2>
        <p>
          The report screen opens your email application with text you can
          review before sending. If you enable the device-information checkbox,
          the draft also contains the device model, manufacturer, Android
          version, and system build information. No report is sent
          automatically, and no audio is attached.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you send an email, Patrik receives your address, message, and any
          information you include, using them to respond and troubleshoot.
          Relevant correspondence may be kept to handle the request and
          follow-up issues; you can ask for its deletion using the contact
          above. Your email provider and Google's email service also process
          correspondence under their policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Opening a website, store page, or privacy link contacts that external
          service and is governed by its policy.
        </p>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can stop audio processing, disable the floating controls, manage
          Android permissions and backups, clear local app data, revisit
          available advertising choices, or use Premium without ads. Contact
          Patrik to request access, correction, or deletion of information you
          have sent directly, or to raise a privacy concern. Requests about
          information held by Google can also be made through Google's privacy
          controls.
        </p>
        <h2>Children and policy updates</h2>
        <p>
          VolEq is a general-purpose audio utility and is not designed for or
          directed to children. If you believe a child has sent personal
          information to Patrik, please use the contact above.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy will be updated when VolEq's data practices change. The
          date above identifies the current policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
